{
"start": 1371.84,
"end": 1375.32,
"speaker_label": "Camille Dubois",
"text": "Which version of the question is truly important?",
"char_start": 5130,
"char_end": 5179,
"unit_id": "t0032.u01",
"sent_id": "t0032.s02"
},
{
"start": 1375.32,
"end": 1378.44,
"speaker_label": "Élodie Chevalier",
"text": "I'm giving you the version that I truly believe in.",
"char_start": 5198,
"char_end": 5249,
"unit_id": "t0033.u01",
"sent_id": "t0033.s01"
},
{
"start": 1378.5,
"end": 1385.22,
"speaker_label": "Élodie Chevalier",
"text": "Risk management in racing isn't about avoiding crashes; it's about choosing which crashes are survivable.",
"char_start": 5250,
"char_end": 5355,
"unit_id": "t0033.u01",
"sent_id": "t0033.s02"
},
{
"start": 1385.28,
"end": 1388.64,
"speaker_label": "Élodie Chevalier",
"text": "We've seen this in teams that use Spoke & Wrench.",
"char_start": 5356,
"char_end": 5405,
"unit_id": "t0033.u01",
"sent_id": "t0033.s03"
},
{
"start": 1388.7,
"end": 1392.3,
"speaker_label": "Élodie Chevalier",
"text": "I've seen this pattern repeat itself in three different teams.",
"char_start": 5406,
"char_end": 5468,
"unit_id": "t0033.u01",
"sent_id": "t0033.s04"
},
{
"start": 1392.3,
"end": 1393.8,
"speaker_label": "Camille Dubois",
"text": "It's settled.\nAlternatively:\nIt's a done deal.\nIt's confirmed.\nIt's arranged.\nIt's agreed.\n(The best option depends on the specific context.)",
"char_start": 5485,
"char_end": 5626,
"unit_id": "t0034.u01",
"sent_id": "t0034.s01"
},
{
"start": 1393.8,
"end": 1402.8,
"speaker_label": "Élodie Chevalier",
"text": "And when teams adopt Spoke & Wrench within this workflow, the trade-off becomes apparent – I've seen this pattern repeat itself in three different teams.",
"char_start": 5645,
"char_end": 5798,
"unit_id": "t0035.u01",
"sent_id": "t0035.s01"
},
{
"start": 1402.8,
"end": 1406.34,
"speaker_label": "Camille Dubois",
"text": "What heuristic do you consistently rely on?",
"char_start": 5815,
"char_end": 5858,
"unit_id": "t0036.u01",
"sent_id": "t0036.s01"
},
{
"start": 1406.4,
"end": 1409.88,
"speaker_label": "Camille Dubois",
"text": "Which version of the question is truly important?",
"char_start": 5859,
"char_end": 5908,
"unit_id": "t0036.u01",
"sent_id": "t0036.s02"
},
{
"start": 1409.88,
"end": 1411.38,
"speaker_label": "Élodie Chevalier",
"text": "That's how I see it.",
"char_start": 5927,
"char_end": 5947,
"unit_id": "t0037.u01",
"sent_id": "t0037.s01"
},
{
"start": 1411.44,
"end": 1418.76,
"speaker_label": "Élodie Chevalier",
"text": "The erosion patterns on the special stages change the choice of racing line between the reconnaissance runs and the actual race day.",
"char_start": 5948,
"char_end": 6080,
"unit_id": "t0037.u01",
"sent_id": "t0037.s02"
},
{
"start": 1418.82,
"end": 1422.42,
"speaker_label": "Élodie Chevalier",
"text": "I saw this pattern repeat itself in three different teams.",
"char_start": 6081,
"char_end": 6139,
"unit_id": "t0037.u01",
"sent_id": "t0037.s03"
},
{
"start": 1680.0,
"end": 1685.34,
"speaker_label": "Camille Dubois",
"text": "Before we conclude, what is one thing that listeners can try this week?",
"char_start": 6156,
"char_end": 6227,
"unit_id": "t0038.u01",
"sent_id": "t0038.s01"
},
{
"start": 1685.34,
"end": 1689.96,
"speaker_label": "Élodie Chevalier",
"text": "Choose one of the ideas we discussed and apply it for two weeks.",
"char_start": 6246,
"char_end": 6310,
"unit_id": "t0039.u01",
"sent_id": "t0039.s01"
},
{
"start": 1690.02,
"end": 1691.88,
"speaker_label": "Élodie Chevalier",
"text": "Everything else is about iteration.",
"char_start": 6311,
"char_end": 6346,
"unit_id": "t0039.u01",
"sent_id": "t0039.s02"
},
{
"start": 1691.88,
"end": 1694.58,
"speaker_label": "Camille Dubois",
